When I gave you those clean logging strings earlier, one of them ("Final Approval (Schedule Overridden)") was **36 characters** long. However, your database table VOUCHER_WORKFLOW strictly limits the LAST_ACTION column to **30 characters** (VARCHAR2(30)), which caused Oracle to reject the insert.
Here is the 2-step fix. We will shorten the strings to look nice, and we will add a permanent safeguard in your logger so this error *never* crashes your app again.
### 1. Update the Logger (The Permanent Safeguard)
We will add a quick .substring(0, 30) to your logWorkflowAction method. This guarantees that no matter what string is passed in the future, it will safely fit in the database without crashing the transaction.
Find your **logWorkflowAction** method and replace it with this:
